Binary bootloader inputs (U-Boot for the Raspberry Pi, a standalone GRUB EFI binary) are looked up by
name in the assets directory and verified against configs/assets.sha256 (modules/assets.sh); there is no
fixed download address. The kernel command line of the Raspberry Pi gets panic=N.

